<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean employers seek to calm striking workers.</title>
<headline>S.Korean employers seek to calm striking workers.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's leading employers' group sought to calm striking workers on Friday, saying companies would only lay off workers if the firms were in &quot;extreme difficulties&quot;.</p>
<p>A new labour law allowing layoffs was rammed through parliament on Thursday. It has sparked strikes that threaten to close much of South Korean industry and key services.</p>
</text>
